  "answer": "A TCP SYN Flood attack works by exploiting the TCP protocol's connection establishment process. In this type of attack, an adversary sends a large number of TCP SYN messages to a target server, which causes the server to allocate resources and maintain state information for each connection attempt. This can overwhelm the server, leading to denial of service for legitimate users who are unable to establish connections due to the server being overloaded with half-open connections [Source 1]. \n\nThe attack requires the ability to generate a significant amount of TCP traffic directed at the target server's port [Source 3].",
